From: Guohan Lu <securely1g@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Install locked Debian archives with real APT/dpkg state

Keep the published rules_distroless .sonic.11 lock importer and compiler fixes.
Add optional apt_install and original :deb exports so OCI images can configure
packages with their own scripts and triggers. For example, ca-certificates
must create its configuration and certificate links, not only extract files.
Original-DEB aliases preserve each lock import's repository prefix, so two
isolated imports each expose the exact reviewed archive they selected.

Installer source: securely1g/rules_distroless PR #2, commit
b3d0573b06b682a7ae3d5de20cc8215b3be3a037, originally registered in closed
sonic-bazel-registry PR #72. Reuse the implementation and tests reviewed in
registry PR #110 plus the lock-prefix integration from PR #114. Apply after
published .sonic.11 patches 0001 through 0013; no existing fix is removed.
This rule installs supplied Debian packages; it does not create DEB packages.

Signed-off-by: Guohan Lu <securely1g@gmail.com>

